{"id":"versehen","lemma":"Versehen","pos":"noun","rank":2394,"glosses":["mistake, oversight"],"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b5/De-Versehen.ogg/De-Versehen.ogg.mp3","gender":"n","forms":{"genitive":"Versehens","plural":"Versehen"},"examples":[{"text":"Es war ein Versehen.","en":"It was an oversight.","words":[{"g":"it"},{"g":"was","l":"sein"},{"g":"a"},null]},{"text":"Jemand hat aus Versehen meine Schuhe genommen.","en":"Someone has taken my shoes by mistake.","words":[{"g":"someone, somebody"},{"g":"has","l":"haben"},{"g":"out of / from"},null,{"g":"my","l":"mein"},{"g":"shoe","l":"Schuh"},{"g":"to take","l":"nehmen"}]},{"text":"Er hat mich aus Versehen geschlagen.","en":"He hit me by mistake.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"has","l":"haben"},{"g":"me","l":"ich"},{"g":"out of / from"},null,{"g":"to beat","l":"schlagen"}]},{"text":"Was heute nacht passiert ist, war ein Versehen.","en":"What happened last night was a mistake.","words":[{"g":"what"},null,null,{"g":"to happen","l":"passieren"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},{"g":"was","l":"sein"},{"g":"a"},null],"phrases":[[1,3,"tonight"]]},{"text":"Sieht dies wie ein Versehen aus?","en":"Does this look like an accident?","words":[{"g":"to see","l":"sehen"},null,{"g":"how"},{"g":"a"},null,{"g":"out of / from"}]}]}